### 1. Webhook deliveries that failed their first try — newest first
POST http://localhost:8080/api/webhook-deliveries/filter
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

{
  "page": 0,
  "size": 20,
  "status": "FAILED",
  "source": "POST_CALL",
  "from": "2026-10-01T00:00:00Z"
}

### 2. Send a FAILED delivery once more
POST http://localhost:8080/api/webhook-deliveries/1/resend
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 3. Developer live SSE stream of webhook deliveries
GET http://localhost:8080/api/webhook-deliveries/listen
Accept: text/event-stream
Authorization: Bearer {{auth_token}}

### 4. LiveKit server webhook (Public, signed)
# Normally only the LiveKit server posts here. The Authorization token is an HS256 JWT signed
# with LIVEKIT_API_SECRET, iss = LIVEKIT_API_KEY, and a "sha256" claim = base64(SHA-256(body)).
# An unsigned request answers 403 LIVEKIT_WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_INVALID.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/webhooks/livekit
Content-Type: application/webhook+json
Authorization: {{livekit_webhook_token}}

{
  "event": "participant_joined",
  "room": { "name": "inbound-_abc123" },
  "participant": {
    "identity": "sip_998901234567",
    "kind": "SIP",
    "attributes": { "sip.phoneNumber": "+998901234567", "sip.trunkPhoneNumber": "+998712000000" }
  }
}
